  "summary": "Convert::ASN1 versions before 0.37 for Perl allow CPU exhaustion via exponent-notation string in INTEGER encoding.",
  "details": "Convert::ASN1 versions before 0.37 for Perl allow CPU exhaustion via exponent-notation string in INTEGER encoding.\n\nThe encoder routes any value with abs >= 2**31 to i2osp without validating that it is an integer. A string in exponent notation such as \"1e8000\" passes that threshold. Math::BigInt expands it to an 8001-digit integer, and i2osp's per-octet conversion loop is quadratic in that size.\n\nAn attacker who controls encoded INTEGER values can exhaust CPU with a short exponent-notation string.",
  "severity": [
    {
      "type": "CVSS_V3",
      "score": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H"
    }
  ],
